@crew pell
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== greet
? endgame:early
- Oi oi, the one who stayed! Biscuit? Half? It's a celebration half.   #funny

== chat
? endgame:early
- I had a whole speech ready for the ramp. A good one. Wasted. I'll save it for Basil.   #funny
? endgame
- No more promotions, eh? Welcome to my world. It's lovely here. Lots of naps.   #funny
- Proper ordinary Tuesday. Pump, lunch, panel, nap. Best kind of day, honestly.
? endgame:early tier>=friend
- Told Mum you stayed. Fourth message this week: "Good. Make them eat." So. Eat.   #funny
? endgame:early tier>=close
- I nearly went, my first month. You nearly went, last week. We're a club now, spanner.   #warm
